  sustainability and community (Cyprus\, EUR 6\,000 fee)
DESCRIPTION:Visual Voices invites artists working at the intersection of ar
 t\, sustainability and community life to the Nicosia Monastery of Arts Res
 idency in Nicosia\, Cyprus. The residency supports site-specific experimen
 tation\, community engagement and public showcases\, with the aim of an ar
 tist-led regeneration of the Walled City of Nicosia and a focus on practic
 es relevant to post-conflict contexts.\n\nOrganisation: Visual Voices (MON
 -ART project\, co-funded by Creative Europe)\nLocation: Walled City of Nic
 osia\, Cyprus (in-person\, shared accommodation)\nAward: EUR 6\,000 artist
  fee per artist\, plus EUR 1\,400 production costs\, travel (EUR 600-1\,00
 0) and shared accommodation. Two artists selected. No application fee stat
 ed.\nDuration: 6 months\, February to July 2027.\n\nMore: https://monart-5
 aee4.web.app/residencies?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral#/residencies/visual-voices-walled-city-of-nicosia-2026
